chapter AFP

session Grounding_Graph = Directed_Cycle_DFS +
  description \<open>Purely graph-theoretic material: extensions of the Isabelle-Graph-Library that
    carry no datalog and no PDDL. Two strands.

    First, \<open>Graph_Topological_Order\<close>: a finite directed graph has a topological numbering iff it
    has no (directed) cycle. This is the mathematical core the datalog foundedness obligation is
    discharged through, but the statement mentions only graphs.

    Second, a whole-graph (linear) directed-cycle search --- the directed counterpart of the
    library's undirected \<open>DFS_Cycles\<close> --- developed as a \<^emph>\<open>chain of refinements\<close>, each level
    removing one set operation from a hot loop and each justified by an equivalence back to the
    level below it. Every level ships an inner pre-seeded DFS (\<open>\<dots>_Aux\<close>) and an outer sweep that
    calls it once per remaining root.

      \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>Level 0\<close> --- \<open>DFS_DirCycle_Linear{_Aux}\<close>, on the library's \<open>DFS_Skeleton\<close> and
        \<open>DFS_DirCycle\<close> unchanged. The reference implementation: the back-edge test recomputes
        \<open>seen - finished\<close> at every skeleton step, and the outer loop recomputes \<open>V - finished\<close>
        at every iteration.
      \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>Level 1\<close> --- \<open>DFS_Skel_More\<close>, which duplicates \<open>DFS_Skeleton\<close> solely to add an
        \<open>on_push\<close> callback, and \<open>DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked{_Aux}\<close> on top of it. The gray (on-stack)
        and unfinished sets become state components maintained incrementally, so both of level 0's
        differences disappear.
      \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>Level 2\<close> --- \<open>DFS_Skel_More_Refine\<close>, \<open>DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked_Aux_Refine\<close> and
        \<open>DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked_Refine\<close> on top of it, where the adjacency map itself moves into the
        state and \<open>on_push\<close> deletes the pushed vertex's in-edges (via a static reverse adjacency
        map fixed by the instance, so the deletions cost one pass over the edges in total). The
        remaining difference, \<open>neighbourhood - seen\<close> (evaluated twice per step), goes too: the
        loop reads a plain neighbourhood. The outer sweep threads that pruned map from one inner
        call to the next, so the pruning is done once over the whole run rather than once per
        root; its state record extends level 1's, and the equivalence back to level 1 is a plain
        equation under the record package's \<open>truncate\<close>, from which soundness and completeness
        transport. The \<^emph>\<open>inner\<close> search needs one assumption the vset ADT does not supply,
        \<open>sel_cong\<close> --- that \<open>sel\<close> is determined by the element set --- because the two levels
        hand \<open>sel\<close> vsets built by different operations; the sweep does not, since it selects
        from the very vset level 1 selects from.

    This session exists to be the graph-library dependency's own layer: everything here belongs
    upstream in the Isabelle-Graph-Library once stable, and keeping it Datalog-free is what makes
    that move a matter of copying files. It is also a cheap prebuilt heap to develop the datalog
    layer on top of.\<close>
  options [timeout = 600]
  sessions
    "Directed_Set_Graphs"
    "Directed_Cycle_DFS"
  theories
    Graph_Topological_Order
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Aux
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear
    DFS_Skel_More
    DFS_Skel_More_Refine
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked_Aux
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked_Equiv
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked_Aux_Refine
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Tracked_Refine
